  "worked_solution": "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{\u2218},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\u2220HQR+m\u2220PQR & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220HQR+{122}^{\u2218} & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220HQR & ={58}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\u25b3QHR$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{\u2218},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\u2220QRH+m\u2220HQR+m\u2220RHQ & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220QRH+{58}^{\u2218}+{90}^{\u2218} & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220QRH+{148}^{\u2218} & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220QRH & ={32}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
